# Copy this file to `.secrets.env` and fill in the values below.
# `.secrets.env` is gitignored; this `.example` is committed as a shape reference.
#
# These are the Worker's PRODUCTION secrets. They are NOT read by `wrangler dev`
# (that uses `.dev.vars` with throwaway literals like AUTH_PASSWORD=local-dev-only).
# `scripts/push-secrets.sh` (npm run secrets:push) reads THIS file and pushes each
# value to Cloudflare via `wrangler secret put`, so secrets are encrypted by
# Cloudflare and never appear in source.
#
# Any value may be a literal OR a 1Password secret reference of the form
# `op://<vault>/<item>/<field>`. push-secrets.sh resolves references via the `op`
# CLI at push time (needs `op signin` or OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN) and leaves
# literals untouched. Surrounding quotes are stripped, so 1Password's
# "Copy Secret Reference" (which includes double quotes) can be pasted verbatim:
#   AUTH_PASSWORD="op://Personal/Obsidian MCP/password"

# Optional. If you have more than one 1Password account, the `op` CLI can't tell
# which one owns the referenced vault. Set the account's sign-in address here so
# push-secrets.sh passes `--account` to `op read`. Not a secret; never pushed.
# OP_ACCOUNT=my.1password.com

# Both secrets must be at least 16 characters (push-secrets.sh refuses anything
# shorter, and the Worker fails closed on a too-short deployed value). Use a long,
# high-entropy value — 32+ random chars recommended, e.g. `openssl rand -base64 32`.

# Required. The shared password typed on the OAuth consent screen each time you
# (re)connect Claude.ai.
AUTH_PASSWORD=

# Optional. Bearer token for the /upload endpoint and HMAC key for signed upload
# links. Leave blank to keep the /upload endpoint and create_upload_link disabled.
UPLOAD_TOKEN=
